.TH XIL\-SFX\-IMPACT "1" "2026\-08\-09" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-sfx\-impact
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-sfx\-impact
[-h] [--show SHOW] [--episode EPISODE] [--output OUTPUT] [--html [HTML]] [--tier {2-minor,3-review,actionable}] [--quiet]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report which source\-backed SFX cues are clipped by duration_seconds, how much audio each loses, and the config change that would restore it. Read\-only — no config is ever modified.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI\,SHOW\/\fR
Restrict to one show slug (default: every show in the workspace)

.TP
\fB\-\-episode\fR \fI\,EPISODE\/\fR, \fB\-\-tag\fR \fI\,EPISODE\/\fR
Restrict to one episode tag (e.g. S01E01)

.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR
CSV output path, or '\-' for stdout (default: reports/sfx_impact_<date>.csv)

.TP
\fB\-\-html\fR \fI\,[HTML]\/\fR
Also write a standalone HTML review page (default path:
reports/sfx_impact_<date>.html)

.TP
\fB\-\-tier\fR \fI\,{2\-minor,3\-review,actionable}\/\fR
Only report cues at this tier ('actionable' = tiers 2 and 3)

.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress the console summary (CSV only)

